WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.468
Russian President Vladimir Putin

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:02.702
making his first visit

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:05.238
to occupied Ukraine since the war began.

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:05.905
I look,

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:07.173
this is video of him

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:08.942
driving through the city of Mariupol,

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:10.977
which Russia occupied last year.

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:11.945
The city suffered

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:13.346
heavy damage and fighting

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:15.015
and became the symbol of Ukraine's

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:17.083
resistance to Moscow's aggression.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:18.218
The Kremlin says Putin

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:19.753
also stopped in their neighborhood

00:00:19.753 --> 00:00:21.087
and spoke to residents.

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.288
They say he was invited

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:23.990
into one of their homes

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:25.091
early on Saturday.

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:26.559
Putin flew to Crimea

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:26.993
to mark

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:27.961
the ninth anniversary

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:30.063
since Russia announced the annexation

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:31.564
of the Ukrainian peninsula.

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:32.599
The move was made after

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:33.700
Russia sent in troops

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.603
and staged a hasty referendum in 2014.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:37.637
Ukraine says

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:39.406
Crimea has been suffering under

00:00:39.406 --> 00:00:40.273
Kremlin rule.

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:41.107
He also said

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:42.108
it's only a matter of time

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:43.476
before all of its occupied

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:45.178
lands are liberated.

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:46.279
CNN's Clare Sebastian

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:48.181
joins us now from London with more.

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:49.382
So Clare, what message

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:50.784
is Putin trying to send here?

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:53.186
What can these visits for

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:55.255
unannounced and come just a day

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:55.688
of course

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:57.157
after an arrest warrant was issued

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:58.825
by the International Criminal Court

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:01.127
against Vladimir Putin himself.

00:01:01.161 --> 00:01:02.328
Obviously with Crimea,

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:02.929
it was designed

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:04.297
to coincide with the anniversary

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:05.131
of that annexation,

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:06.866
the ninth anniversary.

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:09.135
But visiting Mariupol, which we believe

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:10.103
is the first time

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:11.037
he's visited Russian

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:13.206
occupied territories in Ukraine

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:14.908
since the invasion began.

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:16.176
At that may be read

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:18.945
as an act of defiance, a low risk one.

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:19.679
It should be noted,

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:21.514
given that this is Russian occupied

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:23.283
territory, but still,

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:23.516
you know,

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:25.351
thumbing his nose potentially

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:27.420
at that arrest warrant

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.788
in terms of the Russian people

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:31.291
and how this is being presented to them.

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:31.491
Look,

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:32.859
I mean, he's seen behind the car

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:34.461
they're driving from the airport

00:01:34.461 --> 00:01:36.663
in Mariupol towards Mariupol.

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:37.530
We believe

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.565
the last time we saw him buying

00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:39.432
the car was driving

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:40.233
behind the wheel of a car,

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:41.367
was driving a truck

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:43.236
across the Kutch Bridge to Crimea

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:44.904
that was blown up in the autumn

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:47.140
and then partially rebuilt by Russia.

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:49.442
It's designed to protect project control

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:50.910
that he's in charge.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.145
I think there's also an element

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:53.546
of normalizing

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:55.348
these territories as part of Russia.

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:57.317
He's there with the deputy prime minister

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:59.853
Nuland discussing reconstruction

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:01.221
of apartment buildings.

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:03.289
They even visit the Philharmonic,

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.658
which is not far from that drama theater

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:07.093
which was bombed by Russia

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:08.228
almost a year ago

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:10.530
to the day in what is believed to be

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:12.565
the biggest, perhaps mass casualty

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:13.933
event of this war

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:14.400
that you see him

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.635
sitting in the Philharmonic,

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:17.170
the deputy prime minister also noted

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:18.438
that they expect

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:19.572
to have a performance

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:22.075
at the drama theater as soon as April.

00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:24.477
So very much touting their reconstruction

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:25.311
efforts here

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:26.045
because they've been doing

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:27.147
this kind of normalization

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:30.083
with Crimea since 2014.

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:31.618
So I think that's the message

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:33.052
they're trying to get across.

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:34.888
But of course, Ukraine

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:36.389
is making it very clear

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:37.891
that any kind of negotiation with

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:39.993
Russia will have to involve the return

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:41.094
of these territories,

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:42.362
something that Russia is clearly

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:43.363
taking off the table.

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:44.831
All right.

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:45.365
Thanks so much.

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:47.133
Claire Sebastian in London.

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:48.134
Appreciate it.

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:50.970
Now for more on this, I'm joined in Kiev

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.839
by international human rights lawyer

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.440
Wayne Jordache.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.842
Thanks so much for being here with us.

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:57.310
So I want to just start

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:58.178
by getting your reaction

00:02:58.178 --> 00:03:00.113
to what we were just talking about there.

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:00.547
A day

00:03:00.547 --> 00:03:02.782
after the ICC issues an arrest warrant

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.918
for Putin, Putin shows up in Mariupol

00:03:04.918 --> 00:03:05.885
a site of many

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:08.087
alleged war crimes by Russia.

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:10.456
Yes.

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:12.192
I mean that obviously,

00:03:12.192 --> 00:03:13.993
as your previous speaker just said,

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:15.962
some kind of act of defiance,

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:18.097
but a rather empty gesture.

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:19.165
In the end,

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:20.366
the arrest warrants,

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:21.868
which he arrest warrant

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:22.235
he now

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:24.571
faces, will severely restrict

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:26.005
his movement internationally.

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:30.310
So heading to Russian occupied territory,

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.378
which belongs to Ukraine,

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:34.347
may be an act of defiance.

00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:35.648
But as I say,

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:37.050
it doesn't speak to the

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.785
bigger problem he now faces.

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:40.353
All right.

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:41.721
So as a

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:42.522
international human

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:43.256
rights lawyer,

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:44.691
you have a lot of experience

00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:45.959
dealing with the International

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:46.626
Criminal Court.

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:48.828
So how do they make the case

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:49.562
against Putin?

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:50.730
What kind of evidence will

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:53.132
they be relying on here?

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:55.602
Well, for this particular narrow

00:03:55.602 --> 00:03:57.303
set of charges,

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:58.471
which relates

00:03:58.471 --> 00:04:00.540
to the deportation of children

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.108
from Russian occupied territory

00:04:02.108 --> 00:04:03.843
into Russia,

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:04.444
the evidence

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:05.211
really consists

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:07.447
of two or three main points.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.383
Firstly, his public appearances, where he

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:12.819
clearly accepts

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:14.687
along with the commissioner for Human

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:15.455
for Children's

00:04:15.455 --> 00:04:16.022
Rights, who's

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:18.391
also subject to an arrest warrant,

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:22.328
that they are involved in a scheme

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:23.663
of so-called adoption.

00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:26.366
So there's the public admissions

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:27.934
from Putin.

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:30.303
Secondly, there's a presidential decree

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:34.073
which again implicates Putin

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:35.508
and the government in relation

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:37.143
to these adoptions.

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:38.244
And then, of course,

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:39.712
there's the evidence from the ground

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:40.446
that is

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:41.614
thousands of children

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:42.415
going missing

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:44.851
from Russian occupied territory,

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:47.320
many of them with children with parents

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:48.855
and disappearing into Russia.

00:04:48.855 --> 00:04:52.292
So it's the scheme plus the admission

00:04:52.659 --> 00:04:53.993
And I'd also say this

00:04:54.994 --> 00:04:56.062
Putin is

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:56.629
subject to

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:57.563
an arrest warrant

00:04:57.563 --> 00:05:00.133
on the basis of superior responsibility,

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:01.701
which basically means

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:03.836
that he has not prevented

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.572
those crimes or punished them.

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:07.140
And that's

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.341
why his admissions

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:10.243
publicly are so important,

00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:13.980
is essentially approving of these crimes

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:14.814
when he's

00:05:14.814 --> 00:05:16.549
giving these public comments

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:19.352
and therefore admitting to failing

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:20.119
to exercise

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:21.587
his superior responsibility,

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:23.790
which is a really serious issue.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:24.791
Yeah.

00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:26.492
And you were speaking about sort of

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:27.994
those narrow charges,

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:29.228
but obviously there's going to be

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:29.996
many more.

00:05:29.996 --> 00:05:31.664
Your organization has experience

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:32.565
with these

00:05:32.565 --> 00:05:35.635
mobile justice teams to collect evidence

00:05:35.635 --> 00:05:36.569
in cases like these.

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:38.071
So what's involved with that

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:39.872
and what kind of challenges

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:41.908
do you and other investigators face?

00:05:43.443 --> 00:05:45.111
Well, our mobile justice

00:05:45.111 --> 00:05:46.179
teams are essentially

00:05:46.179 --> 00:05:48.414
a support structure for the prosecution

00:05:48.815 --> 00:05:49.615
at the moment.

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:51.351
There are hundreds of prosecutors

00:05:51.351 --> 00:05:53.152
and thousands of police officers

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:54.120
and hundreds of state

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.621
security officers

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:57.623
from Ukraine in the field

00:05:57.623 --> 00:05:59.192
gathering evidence.

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:01.160
And it's a really difficult task.

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:02.061
No one,

00:06:02.061 --> 00:06:03.663
because the volume of crimes

00:06:03.663 --> 00:06:06.132
is absolutely overwhelming.

00:06:06.132 --> 00:06:07.433
Russia's tactics

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:10.670
essentially focus on attacking civilians.

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:11.671
So that gives rise

00:06:11.671 --> 00:06:13.740
to literally thousands

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:15.808
of potential crimes.

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:18.411
Every time an area is liberated, mass

00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:19.712
graves are recovered,

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:21.781
detention facilities are recovered.

00:06:22.515 --> 00:06:24.016
There's forcible displacement,

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:25.618
this theft of children and so on

00:06:25.618 --> 00:06:26.319
and so forth.

00:06:26.319 --> 00:06:28.488
So it's a very difficult job

00:06:28.488 --> 00:06:29.555
on the ground

00:06:29.555 --> 00:06:30.923
to actually collect evidence

00:06:30.923 --> 00:06:33.226
and that's the first phase

00:06:33.226 --> 00:06:34.494
that essentially builds

00:06:34.494 --> 00:06:36.963
a picture of who did what on the ground.

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:38.131
The next phase

00:06:38.131 --> 00:06:39.365
is the most difficult phase,

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:40.266
and that's building up

00:06:40.266 --> 00:06:42.068
the chain of command.

00:06:42.068 --> 00:06:44.137
Who ordered those crimes,

00:06:44.504 --> 00:06:46.139
who facilitated them,

00:06:46.139 --> 00:06:48.074
who planned them, who designed them,

00:06:48.074 --> 00:06:49.876
who controls them? And that

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:52.078
tracking up the chain

00:06:52.078 --> 00:06:56.682
of command is how you implicate people.

00:06:56.682 --> 00:06:58.785
Politicians such as Putin

00:07:00.353 --> 00:07:01.921
And, you know, so

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:02.288
you're saying

00:07:02.288 --> 00:07:04.457
that the volume of the material

00:07:04.457 --> 00:07:05.525
is is daunting.

00:07:05.525 --> 00:07:07.226
But also when it comes to the

00:07:07.226 --> 00:07:08.428
the digital evidence,

00:07:08.428 --> 00:07:10.096
sifting through all of it

00:07:10.096 --> 00:07:11.330
and especially determining

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:11.964
what's real

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:12.632
and what isn't,

00:07:12.632 --> 00:07:15.334
that must be a huge challenge as well.

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:15.835
Well, this

00:07:15.835 --> 00:07:18.171
this is undoubtedly the most documented

00:07:19.205 --> 00:07:21.407
crime base or conflict

00:07:21.808 --> 00:07:23.576
the world has ever seen.

00:07:23.576 --> 00:07:25.945
There are literally thousands

00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:27.447
of organizations

00:07:27.447 --> 00:07:28.881
documenting these crimes.

00:07:28.881 --> 00:07:29.649
And, of course,

00:07:29.649 --> 00:07:31.050
there's a whole prosecution

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:33.119
and judicial apparatus here

00:07:33.119 --> 00:07:34.954
documenting these crimes.

00:07:34.954 --> 00:07:35.521
And, of course,

00:07:35.521 --> 00:07:37.023
we live in the digital age.

00:07:37.023 --> 00:07:39.025
So everything is photographed,

00:07:39.025 --> 00:07:41.394
everything appears on video.

00:07:41.394 --> 00:07:42.462
There's Open-Source

00:07:42.462 --> 00:07:44.030
experts such as Bellingcat

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:46.132
and so on, collecting evidence.

00:07:46.132 --> 00:07:49.368
So it's a really daunting collection.

00:07:49.368 --> 00:07:49.936
Of evidence.

00:07:49.936 --> 00:07:51.270
We're talking about hundreds

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:53.372
of thousands of videos,

00:07:53.372 --> 00:07:54.941
hundreds of thousands of photographs

00:07:54.941 --> 00:07:56.509
and so on and so forth.

00:07:56.509 --> 00:07:58.411
So trying to sift through

00:07:58.411 --> 00:08:00.480
that is going to be the challenge.

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:01.147
Much of that,

00:08:01.147 --> 00:08:03.182
regrettably, will not be that useful

00:08:03.182 --> 00:08:04.383
in a courtroom.

00:08:04.383 --> 00:08:07.286
You're a mature investigator.

00:08:07.787 --> 00:08:10.690
Is can be extremely crucial

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:11.757
to an investigation,

00:08:11.757 --> 00:08:13.426
but much of what they collect

00:08:13.426 --> 00:08:14.293
can also

00:08:14.293 --> 00:08:15.361
be collected in a way

00:08:15.361 --> 00:08:16.863
which is just not admissible

00:08:16.863 --> 00:08:18.831
in a trial process.

00:08:18.831 --> 00:08:20.466
You can't verify the video,

00:08:20.466 --> 00:08:22.502
you can't authenticate photograph.

00:08:23.069 --> 00:08:26.606
You just cannot understand its relevance,

00:08:26.606 --> 00:08:28.341
which probative value.

00:08:28.341 --> 00:08:30.309
So it's a really it's a

00:08:30.309 --> 00:08:31.410
it's a great thing

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:31.777
to have

00:08:31.777 --> 00:08:33.379
all this documentation,

00:08:33.379 --> 00:08:35.414
but it's also a real problem

00:08:35.681 --> 00:08:37.450
in terms of being able to sift through it

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:39.151
and build a case,

00:08:39.151 --> 00:08:41.120
a coherent and robust case.

